*1521 - 5225)/(1521*120) = (7605 - 5225)/(1521*120) = 2380/(1521*120) = 2380/182520. Simplify: 2380/182520. Divide by 20: 119/9126. Divide by 7: 17/1303.8... let me redo. 2380 = 20*119 = 4*5*7*17. 182520 = 1521*120 = 3²*13²*120 = 3²*13²*8*15 = 3²*13²*2³*3*5 = 2³*3³*5*13². So 2380/182520 = (4*5*7*17)/(2³*3³*5*13²) = (4*7*17)/(2³*3³*13²) = (2²*7*17)/(2³*3³*13²) = (7*17)/(2*3³*13²) = 119/(2*27*169) = 119/9126.\n\n119 = 7*17, 9126 = 2*27*169 = 2*3³*13². No common factors. t = 119/9126.\n\nX_y = Q_y + 119t = 4180/507 + 119*(119/9126) = 4180/507 + 14161/9126.\n\n9126 = 18*507. So 4180/507 = 4180*18/9126 = 75240/9126.\nX_y = (75240 + 14161)/9126 = 89401/9126.\n\nX = (5, 89401/9126).\n\nA = (5, 12). AX = |X_y - 12| = |89401/9126 - 12| = |89401/9126 - 109512/9126| = |89401 - 109512|/9126 = 20111/9126.\n\nHmm, let me check sign. 12 = 12*9126 = 109512. 89401 < 109512, so X_y < 12, meaning X is below A. AX = 20111/9126.\n\nSimplify 20111/9126. 9126 = 2*3³*13² = 2*27*169. 20111: is it divisible by 2? No (odd). By 3? 2+0+1+1+1=5, no. By 13? 20111/13 = 1547. 13*1547 = 20111? 13*1500=19500, 13*47=611, total 20111. Yes! So 20111 = 13*1547. 1547/13 = 119. 13*119 = 1547. Yes! So 20111 = 13²*119 = 169*119.\n\n9126 = 2*27*169 = 169*54.\n\nSo AX = (169*119)/(169*54) = 119/54.\n\n119 = 7*17, 54 = 2*27. gcd(119,54)=1. So AX = 119/54. p+q = 119+54 = 173.\n\nLet me verify the computation of X_y more carefully.\n\nt = (5 - Q_x)/120. Q_x = 5225/1521. 5 = 7605/1521. 5 - Q_x = 2380/1521. t = 2380/(1521*120) = 2380/182520.\n\n119*t = 119*2380/182520. 119*2380 = 119*2380. 2380 = 20*119. So 119*2380 = 119*20*119 = 20*119² = 20*14161 = 283220.\n\n283220/182520. Simplify: divide by 20: 14161/9126. Good, matches.\n\nX_y = Q_y + 14161/9126. Q_y = 4180/507 = 4180*18/9126 = 75240/9126.\n\n75240 + 14161 = 89401. X_y = 89401/9126.\n\n12 = 109512/9126. 109512 - 89401 = 20111. AX = 20111/9126 = 119/54.\n\nSo p+q = 173.\n\nLet me double-check the orthocenter. A=(5,12), B=(0,0), C=(21,0). Altitude from A perpendicular to BC (horizontal) → x=5. Altitude from B perpendicular to AC. AC = (16,-12), slope -3/4, perpendicular slope 4/3. y=(4/3)x at x=5 gives y=20/3. H=(5,20/3). ✓.\n\nCheck H is orthocenter: altitude from C perpendicular to AB. AB=(5,12), slope 12/5, perpendicular slope -5/12. Line through C(21,0): y = (-5/12)(x-21). At x=5: y = (-5/12)(-16) = 80/12 = 20/3. ✓.\n\nP: perpendicular bisector of CH. C=(21,0), H=(5,20/3). Midpoint (13, 10/3). CH slope = (20/3)/(5-21) = (20/3)/(-16) = -5/12. Perp slope 12/5. Line: y-10/3 = (12/5)(x-13). At y=0: -10/3 = (12/5)(x-13), x-13 = (-10/3)(5/12) = -50/36 = -25/18. x = 13 - 25/18 = 209/18. ✓.\n\nP = (209/18, 0). PH slope = (20/3 - 0)/(5 - 209/18) = (20/3)/((90-209)/18) = (20/3)/(-119/18) = (20/3)(18/-119) = 360/(-357) = -120/119. ✓.\n\nQ on AB (y=12x/5) and PH. PH: y = (-120/119)(x - 209/18).\n12x/5 = (-120/119)(x - 209/18)\n12x/5 = -120x/119 + (120/119)(209/18)\n(120/119)(209/18) = (20/3)(209/119) = 4180/357.\n12x/5 + 120x/119 = 4180/357.\nx(12*119+120*5)/(5*119) = 4180/357\nx(1428+600)/595 = 4180/357\nx(2028/595) = 4180/357\nx = 4180*595/(357*2028) = 4180*595/(357*2028).\n\n357 = 3*119, 595 = 5*119, so 595/357 = 5/3.\nx = 4180*5/(3*2028) = 20900/6084 = 5225/1521. ✓.\n\nQ_y = 12*5225/(5*1521) = 62700/7605 = 12540/1521 = 4180/507. ✓.\n\nLine through Q perpendicular to PQ (i.e., perpendicular to PH). PH direction (-119, 120) (since slope -120/119). Perp direction (120, 119). Meets AH (x=5).\n\nt = (5 - 5225/1521)/120 = 2380/(1521*120).\nX_y = 4180/507 + 119*2380/(1521*120) = 4180/507 + 119*2380/182520.\n\n119*2380 = 283220. 283220/182520 = 14161/9126.\n4180/507 = 75240/9126.\nX_y = 89401/9126.\nAX = 12 - 89401/9126 = (109512-89401)/9126 = 20111/9126 = 119/54.\n\np+q = 173.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1787242574}
